e-network-architecture walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the segmentation design review authored and self-reviewed in-session.

Scope: fictional Harborlight Manufacturing (450 employees, 2 plants, corporate HQ;
  flat network, OT reachable from workstations, vendors on employee VPN).
Artifacts authored:
  - Current-state inventory: actors (employees, operators, vendors, remote engineers,
    R&D/GPU cluster), assets (ERP/payroll, PLCs, file shares, training data + model
    weights, order data); headline finding: no trust boundary between corporate IT
    and plant floor.
  - Zone map: 8 zones (corporate users, data-center services, DMZ, plant OT,
    R&D/AI training, management, guest Wi-Fi, vendor access) each with a one-line
    trust statement.
  - Boundary table (excerpt): corporate->DC, DMZ->interior, corporate->OT
    (deny-by-default; historian read-only feed out; 2 named engineering
    workstations in via jump host), AI zone (deny all but ingest/export paths),
    management zone (admin workstations only, MFA, encrypted).
  - Zero-trust decisions mapped to SP 800-207 tenets: per-session vendor grants
    (tenet 3), NAC posture checks (tenet 5), encrypted inter-zone traffic (tenet 2),
    named trust-algorithm inputs per zone (tenet 4).
  - NAC placement: 802.1X on wired + corporate Wi-Fi; quarantine for unknowns;
    MAC-bypass exceptions inventoried and named.
  - Vendor/remote access: isolated vendor segment, MFA, time-bounded, session
    recording; VPN concentrator at edge landing in remote-access zone.
  - Monitoring points: IDS on SPAN at edge, DMZ boundaries, OT boundary,
    AI-zone boundary — detection goal stated per sensor.
  - Decision log: every boundary decision with owner/date; phase-2
    micro-segmentation deferred with owner + revisit date.

Self-review checklist (2026-10-10):
  [x] every boundary has an enforcement mechanism (no decorative zones)
  [x] DMZ->interior boundary as strict as internet-facing (no trust inward)
  [x] management plane isolated in its own zone
  [x] third-party access never lands in employee zones (per-session, recorded)
  [x] OT zone has no internet path; AI training zone treated as high-value
      micro-segmentation target with exfiltration as primary threat
  [x] tenets cited against verified SP 800-207 text (tenets 1-7, PE/PA/PEP,
      trust algorithm, deployment models, migration steps 7.3.1-7.3.5)
  [x] no invented statistics; company labeled fictional throughout
  [x] differentiated from a-tcpip-ports (decisions, not packet mechanics)
Nothing unrun: worked-case lessons have no CLI steps to mark.
